UID:10038722-1794643200-1794661200@thedirt.online
SUMMARY:Davis Farmers Market
DESCRIPTION:Year-round at Central Park in downtown Davis\, thousands gather each week to shop for what is grown\, raised\, and made locally at our markets. We are dedicated to bringing farmers right to your table\, so we stay open rain or shine. \nWalk rows of stalls lined with an array of fruits and vegetables\, including certified organic produce\, choice meats\, chicken\, seafood\, wine\, local eggs and honey. Choose from a variety of fresh-baked goods\, plants\, flowers and gifts. Enjoy a picnic from one of our many food stands\, made from market ingredients. \nSee the vendor list here: https://www.davisfarmersmarket.org/our-sellers/ \nFarmers Market Hours  \nCentral Park: Saturdays 8a–1p (year-round)\, and Wednesdays 3p–6p (September through March); 4p–8p (April through August)\nUC Davis – North Quad: Wednesdays 10a–1:30p (fall and spring quarters)\nSutter Davis Hospital: Thursdays 10a–1p (May through September)\nSutter Medical Center\, Sacramento: Thursdays 2:30p–5:30p \n 
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/davis-farmers-market-3-2-2-2-2/2026-11-14/
LOCATION:Central Park
CATEGORIES:Bring the Kids,Food & Drink,Shopping
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/davis-farmers-market-logo-KERN-ADJUST2-01-1-e1649900473633.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Davis Farmers Market":MAILTO:dfmpr@dcn.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_davisbikeclubwww
SUMMARY:Second Saturday Explorer Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T130000
DTSTAMP:20261114T061352Z
UID:no2an62sdfnbv3lbl0dk4l37so@google.com__20261114
SEQUENCE:3
CREATED:20251104T152227Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>For the November second Saturday Explorer ride\, my plan is
  to follow an approximately 53 mile loop starting in Knights Landing at 9:
 30 a.m. that will eventually take us to Dunnigan\, our lunch stop. We will
  eat at Dunnigan Community Park. Bring your own lunch or plan to purchase 
 food at the Zamora mini-mart or the Chevron Station in Dunnigan (sadly\, i
 t seems that the Jack-in-the-Box in Dunnigan has closed). On the way back 
 we might see winter water birds along County Line Road and CA-45. Substant
 ial chance of rain will cancel the ride.<u></u><u></u></p><p>At a minimum\
 , regroups will be at the following locations and intersections:<u></u><u>
 </u></p><ul><li>Zamora Mini-Mart<u></u><u></u></li><li>Rd 14 and Rd 85<u><
 /u><u></u></li><li>Rd 85 and Rd 8<u></u><u></u></li><li>Chevron at Rd 6 an
 d Rd 89<u></u><u></u></li><li>Rd 89 and County Line Rd<u></u><u></u></li><
 li>County Line Rd and CA-45<u></u><u></u></li></ul><p>Please let me know i
 f you need additional information or have suggestions for route improvemen
 ts.</p><br>Ride Description: <a href="https://davisbikeclub.org/2nd-sat-e
 xplorer-ride/" target="_blank">https://davisbikeclub.org/2nd-sat-explorer-
 ride/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T154736Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Davis Bike Club
X-SOURCE-URL:https://davisbikeclub.org/club-events-calendar/
END:VEVENT
