BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UC Davis CampusGroups": "https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=909817"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_campusgroups
SUMMARY:Freedom of Expression at UC Davis: Know Your Rights
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261124T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261124T150000
UID:8f5a67631a2b5e3f820eb44eba1392c610212026_2:15:15_PM@campusgroups.com
DESCRIPTION:Ever wondered where the line is between free speech\, campus p
 olicy\, and taking a stand? Whether you're planning a demonstration\, orga
 nizing an event with your RSO\, or just navigating lively debates around c
 ampus\, knowing your rightsis key.\n\nJoin CSI's Assistant Director for St
 udent Expression\, Jose Napoles\, for an interactive breakdown of what Fre
 edom of Expression actually looks like on campus. We’ll clear up the con
 fusion around campus forums\, break down time\, place\, and manner policie
 s\, and give you the tools to make informed decisions and keep your commun
 ities safe.\n\nIn this session\, you’ll learn how to:\n\nKnow Your Forum
 s: Understand the difference between public\, limited\, and nonpublic spac
 es on campus and how your rights shift in each.\n\nDecode Campus Policies:
  Get the real scoop on policy boundaries like amplified sound\, tabling\, 
 and event security so your events run smoothly.\n\nProtect & Advocate: Dis
 cover how the Student Affairs Response Team supports student expression\, 
 helps de-escalate tension\, and connects you with key campus resources.\n\
 nNavigate Real Scenarios: Work through practical examples of campus dissen
 t and learn proactive strategies for community safety and self-care.\n\nWh
 o should attend? Student organization leaders\, campus advocates\, and any
  Aggie who wants to speak up\, stay informed\, and make an impact effectiv
 ely.\n\nBring your questions and come learn more about Freedom of Expressi
 on at UC Davis.\n\n*SPACE IS LIMITED!*
URL:https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=909817
X-SOURCE:UC Davis CampusGroups
END:VEVENT
